<!--
  Sample policy for an API proxy that wants to call one of the six
  ISAM-* type-specific shared flows, e.g. attached in PreFlow before the
  proxy's own target logic. Attach exactly the ONE type your proxy needs;
  pick SharedFlowBundle from:

    ISAM-SAML-Light        type 1: no bearer token, client cert only
    ISAM-SAML-User         type 2: WS-Trust, user SAML, with bearer token
    ISAM-SAML-TP           type 3: WS-Trust, tp/third-party SAML, with bearer token
    ISAM-SAML-Technical    type 4: WS-Trust, technical SAML, with bearer token
    ISAM-JWT-SAML          type 5: JSON request, SAML assertion in JSON response
    ISAM-JWT-Token         type 6: JSON request, JWT itself is the token (no SAML)

  Optional (types 1-5 only; type 6 has no compression): set compressSaml as
  a flow variable before this step to override that type's KVM default for
  this one request:

    <AssignVariable>
        <Name>compressSaml</Name>
        <Value>true</Value>
    </AssignVariable>

  After this step runs:
    - Types 1-5 (SAML-bearing): the shared flow has already set request
      headers X-SAML-Assertion (base64, zipped or plain per compressSaml),
      X-SAML-Assertion-Compressed (true/false), and X-SAML-Subject-Id. Flow
      variables saml.assertion.xml, isam.exchanged.subject.id,
      isam.exchanged.assertion.notBefore/.notOnOrAfter, saml.assertion.output,
      saml.signature.valid (true by the time this step returns, since
      RF-SAML-Signature-Invalid would otherwise have raised a fault), and
      saml.signature.cert.subject/.issuer/.thumbprint are also available if
      you'd rather read them directly.
    - Type 6 (JWT-only): the shared flow has set X-Access-Token and
      X-Access-Token-Type request headers directly; no signature/compression
      variables exist for this type since none of that applies. Flow
      variables isam.exchanged.token/.token.type/.token.expiresIn are also
      available.

  Any fault before this step completes (missing config/bearer token/client
  cert, both ISAM hosts down, bad response, invalid signature) propagates up
  as a raised fault; handle it in this proxy's DefaultFaultRule/FaultRules
  as needed.
-->
<FlowCallout name="FC-ISAM-Exchange">
    <DisplayName>FC ISAM Exchange</DisplayName>
    <SharedFlowBundle>ISAM-SAML-User</SharedFlowBundle>
</FlowCallout>
